{{-- Breadcrumbs for the marketing pages.

     Reads two things from the including page: `breadcrumbs`, an array of
     `{ label, href? }` with the deepest last, and `breadcrumbWidth`, the
     container width of that page's own content. The last entry is the current
     page and carries no link, because a link to where you already are is a link
     nobody wants.

     The width is passed in rather than fixed here because the prose pages are
     narrower than the card grids, and a trail that does not start above the
     heading it belongs to reads as a stray line of text.

     A partial rather than a component. The stated reason used to be that stx
     dropped props passed component to component, so shared chrome built as a
     component rendered empty, and that is why the rest of this app uses
     partials too.

     That is fixed as of stx 0.2.395, checked by rendering a
     page -> Outer -> Inner chain: the inner component receives the page's prop
     intact. So the reason no longer holds, here or for the other partials, and
     anyone reading it as a constraint should stop.

     What is left is a preference rather than a blocker. `<Breadcrumb>` renders
     the same semantics this does, and would take `breadcrumbWidth` through
     className, which lands on the <nav> (a width competes with nothing, so the
     append-order caveat in stacksjs/stx#1993 does not bite here). analyticshq
     already calls the component from its own breadcrumb partial. --}}
<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="px-6 pt-8 mx-auto {{ breadcrumbWidth }}">
  <ol class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 items-center list-none text-sm text-subtle">
    @foreach (breadcrumbs as crumb)
      @if (!loop.first)
        {{-- Decorative, so it is hidden from a screen reader, which gets the
             list structure instead. --}}
        <li aria-hidden="true" class="text-line">/</li>
      @endif

      <li>
        @if (crumb.href)
          <a href="{{ crumb.href }}" class="no-underline text-muted hover:text-ink">{{ crumb.label }}</a>
        @else
          <span aria-current="page" class="text-ink">{{ crumb.label }}</span>
        @endif
      </li>
    @endforeach
  </ol>
</nav>
